  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\nA moist westerly flow aloft continues to reside over MT this\nmorning. This will result in another day of cool temperatures,\nmostly cloudy skies and a small chance for a light rain shower,\nmostly over North Central MT. There is not a lot of upper level\nsupport for the showers today, thus any rainfall should be \nlighter than yesterday. \n\nAfter a cool day today, expect afternoon temperatures to rise/fall\nabout 4 to 8 degrees daily over the next few days. So we will have\na mix of warm/cool days starting this weekend and going into early\nnext week. \n\nWeak upper level ridging on Monday, combined with a bit stronger\nwesterly winds will allow for a warm day, with some areas\napproaching record high temperatures for this time of year.\nElevated fire conditions are possible on Monday because of the low\nhumidity, increased winds and warm temperatures.\n\nLittle to no precipitation is currently forecast from this Friday\nwell into next week. It is looking like the next chance for some \nmore widespread precipitation might be next Thu/Fri when an upper \nlevel disturbance is forecast to move southward through the CWA.\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\nOverall the chance for record high temperatures on Monday is the\nmain impact weather over the next few days. Brusda",
